  },
  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "1914-root",
    "title": "Pronunciation - The Queen's English",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "How important is the accent you use when speaking English?",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "bdd3d85f02d55b30",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "1914-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/1914-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "Pronunciation - The Queen's English"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How important is the accent you use when speaking English? Many English language learners feel they need to sound more 'British' or 'American' when they could be focusing on other, more important, aspects of their pronunciation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Queen's English, also known as Received Pronunciation (RP), is still regarded by some as the most \"correct\" way to speak English. Whilst only spoken by approximately "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "2% of the British population",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://www.theguardian.com/science/shortcuts/2018/may/22/received-pronunciation-may-be-dying-out-but-its-passing-is-long-overdue",
                    "target": "_self",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", some language learners focus their efforts on copying this accent. In the past, BBC (British Broadcasting Corporation) news presenters, politicians and public figures in the UK would be expected to use RP as an indication of their social status and educational background. However, over time, standard English has become much more popular, and these days a much more "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "diverse range of accents",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zoJ45vPAQFQ",
                    "target": "_self",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " can be commonly heard on the TV and radio stations in the UK."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Instead of worrying about your accent, focus on improving other aspects of your pronunciation, such as rhythm, word stress, sentence stress, intonation and chunking. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Watch this video by the British Council",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=108&v=UawwTSzaZzk",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " for useful tips on improving your pronunciation and then try out the websites and apps recommended below to practise."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list_item",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "ELSA",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "http://www.elsaspeak.com/home",
                            "target": "_self",
                            "linktype": "url",
                            "uuid": null,
                            "anchor": null,
                            "custom": {}
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is a free app which gives you automatic feedback on your pronunciation using speech recognition technology. "
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list_item",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "BBC Learning English",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "http://www.bbc.co.uk/learningenglish/english/features/pronunciation",
                            "target": "_self",
                            "linktype": "url",
                            "uuid": null,
                            "anchor": null,
                            "custom": {}
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " provides short videos on improving your pronunciation of specific consonant and vowel sounds."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list_item",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Youglish",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "http://youglish.com/",
                            "target": "_self",
                            "linktype": "url",
                            "uuid": null,
                            "anchor": null,
                            "custom": {}
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " allows you to check the natural pronunciation of any word by searching Youtube videos and presenting it in context."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
